# Scenario diag-stic-fgbg-pass (plan 06-13, D-20, A-04, D-19): outcome pass, exit 0. The third original
# diagnostic with no controller input: the first read of 01FE returns the low byte FF, so the program
# stays in Foreground/Background mode, enables the display, copies four card patterns to graphics RAM,
# fills BACKTAB, writes six explicit card words, waits and halts (about tick 88,500, a hand estimate that
# no assert uses; the first frame ends at tick 59,736 and the second at 119,472, so the guest is still
# running when frame 0 completes and has stopped before frame 1 completes). The asserts are the
# hand-derived expectations of data/golden/diag-stic-fgbg-pass.expect (derivation in
# docs/video/diag-stic-1-derivation.md and data/video/frames/F-D1.frame, written before the program);
# they are the same lines in the same order (golden-expect-drift). The installed consumer of plan 06-13
# replays the same image with no events.
ivss 1
id diag-stic-fgbg-pass
profile intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
content exec boot-stub
content grom zero-grom
content cart diag-stic-1.ivsc
capture video 0 1
run-to 150000 ticks stop halted
assert halted == yes
assert mem 02F0 == 03C5
assert mem 02F1 == 00FF
assert mem 02A3 == 2A01
assert mem 02A4 == 0E0A
assert mem 02A5 == 1A13
assert mem 02A6 == 381C
assert mem 02DC == 2C1D
assert mem 02EF == 1C0F
assert mem 0200 == 0000
assert frame 0 displayed == yes
assert frame 0 pixel 0 0 == 0
assert frame 0 pixel 158 0 == 0
assert frame 0 pixel 24 64 == 1
assert frame 0 pixel 24 65 == 5
assert frame 0 pixel 33 65 == 3
assert frame 0 pixel 41 65 == 3
assert frame 0 pixel 49 64 == 12
assert frame 0 pixel 0 88 == 5
assert frame 0 pixel 1 88 == 6
assert frame 0 pixel 152 88 == 7
assert frame 0 pixel 158 95 == 7
assert frame 0 pixel 153 89 == 10
assert frame 0 hash == 86b80eb73c51152ac252a1bbebcc86ead4535ac9ebdbf2a346bd8bf1b0383596
assert video count == 1
